#!/bin/sh
# /init has already mounted /dev, /sys and /proc. The 00- prefix runs this
# before udev's global coldplug/settle. Hardware discovery uses sysfs rather
# than a udev symlink, and the real root need not have been mounted.
case "${1:-}" in
  prereqs) exit 0 ;;
esac

# A missing or failed cosmetic display must never stop the device booting.
# gbsplash bounds device discovery itself and leaves the completed frame intact.
[ -x /usr/local/lib/gamebird/gbsplash ] || exit 0
[ -r /etc/gamebird/boot-splash.conf ] || exit 0
. /etc/gamebird/boot-splash.conf
log=/dev/null
[ ! -w /dev/kmsg ] || log=/dev/kmsg
# Module/firmware failure must also be bounded. Names are validated and generated
# by the installer. The normal path waits only for the real driver initialization.
/usr/local/lib/gamebird/gbsplash-timeout --signal=TERM --kill-after=1 3 /bin/sh -c \
  'for module do modprobe "$module" || exit; done' sh $GBSPLASH_MODULES \
  >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
/usr/local/lib/gamebird/gbsplash-timeout --signal=TERM --kill-after=1 3 /usr/local/lib/gamebird/gbsplash \
  --image /usr/share/gamebird/boot/splash.rgb565 --timeout-ms 1200 \
  >/dev/null 2>"$log" || :
exit 0
